    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nUsing the standard algorithm, we can calculate the difference between two numbers containing any number of digits.\n\nContent:\nLet's use the standard algorithm to compute the following difference:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 42,345 - 3,124]\n\nContent:\nFirst, we line up our numbers (ones over ones, tens over tens, hundreds over hundreds, and so on):\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4|2|3|4|5; \u2212|3|1|2|4]\n\nContent:\nNext, we proceed by subtracting the numbers in each place value from right to left, borrowing where needed.\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 3|12; 4|2|3|4|5; \u2212|3|1|2|4; 3|9|2|2|1]\n\nContent:\nTherefore,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 42,345 - 3,124 = 39,221.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Subtracting Numbers Up to Five Digits Without Borrowing\n\nExample Prompt:\nCompute the value of [MATH: 57,458 - 25,242.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 5|7|4|5|8; \u2212|2|5|2|4|2]\n\nNext, we proceed by subtracting the numbers in each place value from right to left:\n\n[MATH: 5|7|4|5|8; \u2212|2|5|2|4|2; 3|2|2|1|6]\n\nTherefore,\n[MATH: 57,458 - 25,242 = 32,216.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 44, 236 \u2212 21, 023 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 21, 321]\nb. [MATH: 23, 123]\nc. [MATH: 22, 123]\nd. [MATH: 23, 323]\ne. [MATH: 23, 213]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 12, 747 \u2212 2, 515 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 10, 352]\nb. [MATH: 9, 579]\nc. [MATH: 10, 232]\nd. [MATH: 9, 759]\ne. [MATH: 10, 252]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Subtracting Numbers Up to Five Digits With Borrowing\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 83,005 - 52,009?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 8|3|0|0|5; \u2212|5|2|0|0|9]\n\nNext, we proceed by subtracting the numbers in each place value from right to left, borrowing where needed.\n\n[MATH: 2|9|9|15; 8|3|0|0|5; \u2212|5|2|0|0|9; 3|0|9|9|6]\nTherefore,\n[MATH: 83,0